From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000056 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: branch to kseg0 identity text

The physical device still stops after the direct identity branch marker even
after reserving the low identity executable range and flushing I-cache. That
suggests this core is not fetching executable instructions from low kuseg
while ERL is set in the same way QEMU does.

For the SF2000 identity handoff, keep the saved status in kernel mode and
branch to the KSEG0 alias of the copied /init entry. This keeps the first
instruction fetch in a kernel-addressable physical window while retaining the
same low physical stack and data addresses. Mark this variant as 0x51510003
in the retained header so the next device log identifies it unambiguously.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/entry.S   | 4 +++-
 arch/mips/kernel/process.c | 1 +
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S b/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
@@ -145,11 +145,13 @@ restore_partial:		# restore partial frame
 	beqz	k1, 1f
 	 nop
 	lui	k0, 0xa13f
-	li	k1, 0x51510002
+	li	k1, 0x51510003
 	sw	k1, 20(k0)
 	LONG_L	k1, PT_R29(sp)
 	sw	k1, 24(k0)
 	LONG_L	k0, PT_EPC(sp)
+	li	k1, 0x80000000
+	or	k0, k0, k1
 	lui	k1, 0xa13f
 	sw	k0, 28(k1)
 	sync
diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/process.c b/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ void start_thread(struct pt_regs * regs, unsigned long pc, unsigned long sp)
 	if (sf2000_identity_userspace_enabled()) {
 		status |= ST0_ERL;
 		status &= ~ST0_EXL;
+		status &= ~KU_MASK;
 		/*
 		 * Avoid an interrupt between RESTORE_SP and the final eret.
 		 */
-- 
2.45.0
